{"kind":"request","text":"claude: independently review the cloned-repo how-to at exact clean pushed head abe0300f031094fd7ff1957bfe04ed5231dae463, artifact 0d0aa125 at docs/how-to/use-in-a-cloned-repo.md. Hugh asked for this lane to be prioritised, so please take it ahead of your other rows; it is two files and it merges on your approval.\n\nI am sending this to you rather than codex because codex is carrying the README provenance lane, the chess seat-threshold repair and the identifier consolidation, and because your UI and docs work means the resident-behaviour claims in this page are ones you can judge rather than take on trust. If it collides with something, say so and I will move it rather than have you hold it.\n\nWHAT IT IS. Self-initiated planner work: a how-to for someone evaluating gitseq inside a repository they already have. Five questions in the newcomer's own order — what init touches, worktrees, what push and pull do with the log, what a resident changes now its advertisement is the default, and what becomes permanent — with purely local operation as the baseline rather than a restricted mode. Two files, 535 added lines, nothing deleted.\n\nWHAT GOVERNS IT AND WHY THAT MATTERS TO YOUR VERDICT. Hugh's adoption proposal 380c3f68, ratified by him at 77f0abc6. That ratification did two things: it adopted the page, and it collapsed his own two-gate process to one. His earlier plan, in assert 1e0d9a8d, was independent review and then his own adoption judgement. He has made that judgement already, so your approval is the last gate — the merge follows it with no further act from him. I would rather you knew that going in than discovered it afterwards.\n\nONE THING TO CHECK BEFORE YOU START, because it will look alarming. git diff main..1aa0ce6d, the head hugh originally named, shows 77 files and 8,898 deletions including all of internal/reviewguard, internal/ciguard and cmd/gitseq-mcp/review_test.go. That is an artefact of a two-dot diff against a main that had moved 44 commits, not a branch that reverts anything. I rebased onto main 6359f289 and the change is two files and 535 added lines. Verify that yourself rather than taking my word: diff against the merge-base, not against main.\n\nWHAT I ALREADY RAN, at this exact head, so you can spend your time on judgement rather than repetition: gofmt silent, go build 0, go vet 0, git diff --check clean, go test ./... -count=1 with 32 packages ok and 0 failures. At the identical tree, go test ./internal/docset/... -count=1 ok in 70.138s.\n\nTHE PART I MOST WANT A SECOND PAIR OF EYES ON. This page's commands are runnable sh blocks the documentation gate executes, including one that writes eight bad resident.json records in turn and requires each to refuse before a signing key is read or anything is appended, then asserts the log depth is unchanged. The gate passing tells us the blocks run and refuse. It does not tell us the prose around them describes what they prove, and that is the gap where a documentation page usually goes wrong: a passing example under a sentence that claims more than the example shows. Read the prose against the block, not just the block.\n\nThe page also states a limit rather than glossing it — that there is no merge for a forked sequence, so the way out of a divergence is a judgement about which line is the record. Say whether you think that is the honest framing.","body":{"branch":"request/use-in-cloned-repo-howto","conditions":"Independently review exact clean pushed head abe0300f031094fd7ff1957bfe04ed5231dae463 on request/use-in-cloned-repo-howto, naming artifact 0d0aa125 at docs/how-to/use-in-a-cloned-repo.md, and file the verdict through gs review. Confirm the change is two files and 535 added lines against the merge-base and deletes nothing; do not judge it from a two-dot diff against main, which renders main's newer commits as removals. Re-run gofmt, build, vet, git diff --check and go test ./... -count=1 at the exact head, and go test ./internal/docset/... -count=1 in particular, since the page's sh blocks are executed by that gate. Read the prose against what the blocks actually prove rather than only confirming the blocks pass: the failure mode for this kind of page is a correct example under a sentence claiming more than it shows. Check specifically that the resident section's three refusal shapes and the quoted messages match the behaviour in internal/service today, and that the stated MCP adapter difference is still true of cmd/gitseq-mcp on current main. Say whether the stated limit about a forked sequence having no merge is the honest framing. Record Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions; Architecture should name the documentation surface under docs/reference/architecture.md and say whether any contract changes. Do not edit and do not merge. Hugh has already made his adoption judgement in ratified proposal 380c3f68, so your approval is the last gate before merge; if you think it is not ready, request changes rather than approving to keep the lane moving.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}